Whenever

00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:25.670
l sing a song

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:29.270
l hear a voice coming from the microphone

00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:31.730
wishing me the best

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:34.450
l want you

00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:36.010
to hear it too

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:36.860
Good luck!

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.810
You can't show your love

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:46.540
just with niceties

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:51.420
That won't provide comfort

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:55.690
Whenever l say something

00:00:58.130 --> 00:01:01.730
out of the ordinary

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:05.180
in my heart

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:07.680
l wish you the best

00:01:07.870 --> 00:01:10.230
l want you

00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:11.850
to hear that line

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:12.690
Good luck!

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:38.880
Temporary
Park Closure

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:46.350
Oh no, what's happening?

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:48.770
I think we're going to derail.

00:01:48.770 --> 00:01:50.180
Wow! Then what?

00:01:51.190 --> 00:01:53.270
We'll probably fall.

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:56.820
Wow, wow! Then what?

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:03.660
We're all going to die!

00:02:06.830 --> 00:02:08.700
Captain!

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:09.950
Everyone...

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:12.330
Nozomi!

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:14.460
Masami!

00:02:18.170 --> 00:02:19.460
Those are...

00:02:21.470 --> 00:02:24.840
I think you know very well what will happen if their ride isn't stopped,

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:26.350
Utoku Masami.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:30.310
You don't have time to get Maccha Green.

00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:33.270
I thought for sure Maccha would be the one to come, though.

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:35.310
You can't do this, Shigyo!

00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:36.860
According to the Twin Tower Declaration,

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:38.150
the time and place must be decided at least a day in adva—

00:02:38.150 --> 00:02:39.230
Oh, <i>so sorry</i>.
the time and place must be decided at least a day in adva—

00:02:39.230 --> 00:02:40.610
Oh, <i>so sorry</i>.

00:02:40.610 --> 00:02:43.570
Messages get lost <i>so</i> easily these days.

00:02:43.570 --> 00:02:47.320
Enough of that. How do you plan on getting yourself out of <i>this one</i> without a Best?

00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:51.120
Th-That's fine! We still have our ultimate weapon!

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:52.540
We'll just call it out again!

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:56.750
Are you talking about that Hyper Maccha Robot from yesterday?

00:02:56.750 --> 00:02:58.460
Yeah! You scared yet?!

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:00.960
Well, it's right over there.

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:05.680
Wh—

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:08.180
Just for the record,

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:10.930
we totally wouldn't get played by something like that.

00:03:10.930 --> 00:03:12.850
What? But you were crapping your pants yester—

00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:14.480
Nuh-uh! It was all part of the plan!

00:03:26.410 --> 00:03:31.120
With Maccha Green out of the picture, there's not much you can do.

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:33.500
If you want to save your precious squad members,

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:36.670
you'll surrender to us right now.

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:39.500
Captain...

00:03:40.130 --> 00:03:43.800
